unexpected expression: struct_tag
found no match for symbol 'swap'
\* identifier: std::tag-__not_<
--
Matching `goto-cc` reproducer for the libstdc++ SFINAE-leak bug
documented in cbmc-cpp/cpp11_std_is_swappable_sfinae.

User-visible symptoms of the bug (reported as "goto-cc ~/harness.cpp
should work today but both yields debug output and just doesn't
work"):

1. `goto-cc` writes spurious `error: unexpected expression:
   struct_tag` diagnostics to stderr when `#include <array>`
   transitively instantiates `std::__is_swappable_impl<T>`.  Per
   [temp.deduct]/8 these substitution failures must be absorbed
   silently during overload resolution — no user-visible error
   may be emitted.

2. The error diagnostic itself embeds an `irep::pretty()` dump
   (indented sub-fields with `* #source_location:`, `* line:`,
   `* identifier:` entries) rather than a clean source-level
   message.  This is the "debug output" referenced by the user.

The test ships a minimum-size reproducer that exercises the bug
via `goto-cc` (chain.sh builds with goto-cc then runs cbmc on the
resulting .gb).  `std::array<double, 3>` is chosen because it is
the smallest `std::array` instantiation that triggers the
SFINAE-leak code path.

Fix expectations:
 * No `error:` line in the combined stdout/stderr.
 * No `irep::pretty()` indented-sub-field dump in the output.
 * `VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL` from cbmc.
